---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/alternatives/yotpo-email-sms-alternative";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS alternatives: restore messaging, retain useful dependencies";
const desc = "Accept supported messaging after Yotpo retirement while preserving Reviews, Loyalty, capture, sender and customer record ownership.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Yotpo Email & SMS still a new messaging option?",
    "answer": "The migration announcement scheduled full deprecation for December 31, 2025, and the current SMS notice reports inactive dashboard and background services. Evaluate supported replacements."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must Reviews and Loyalty move with messaging?",
    "answer": "Evaluate them separately. Preserve useful retained products and prove the replacement receives required identifiers, current values and events without duplicate requests."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if the old records are unavailable?",
    "answer": "Document missing evidence and responsible recovery contacts. Keep unresolved permissions excluded and validate the supported destination without promising recovery or reactivation."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <article class="container py-16 prose-shopify">
    <a href="/alternatives">All alternatives</a>
    <h1>{title}</h1>
    <p>Replacing retired messaging is a continuity project. Keep supported delivery operating while resolving missing records, broken capture routes and retained product dependencies. Reviews and Loyalty can remain useful without making the former messaging bundle a current sending option.</p>
    <h2>Use the retirement record to frame the decision</h2>
    <p><a href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo’s migration announcement</a> scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025 and named Attentive and Omnisend as partners. The current <a href="https://smsbump.com/get-started">SMS lifecycle notice</a>, checked November 25, 2026, says its dashboard and background services are inactive. A current procurement brief needs supported messaging; do not propose a new parallel trial against the retired service.</p><p>The <a href="/apps/yotpo-email-sms">historical app review</a> inventories the transition. This page decides what the supported replacement must own now. Vendor partner guidance is a place to start a demonstration, not evidence that your integration or old promotional offer remains available. If a replacement already works, investigate the remaining exceptions without restarting all delivery.</p>
    <h2>Keep Reviews and Loyalty ownership explicit</h2>
    <p>Yotpo continues to present Reviews and Loyalty products in its current product navigation. Retaining review content, storefront widgets, rewards and referral relationships can avoid unnecessary disruption when they still serve the store. Messaging retirement alone does not require moving them.</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Retained job</th><th>Replacement boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Review request</td><td>One sender per order; retained product records the submitted review</td></tr><tr><td>Reward reminder</td><td>Identify who calculates balance, provides a valid reward link and cancels stale reminders</td></tr><tr><td>Referral invitation</td><td>Preserve the referral destination and its customer key</td></tr><tr><td>Storefront widget</td><td>Keep display ownership separate from message delivery</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Demonstrate an earned reward, redemption, refund and tier change through the actual connector. Inspect changed values before a queued message releases. Do not run duplicate loyalty accrual merely to compare senders. If the destination lacks a required field, change the message or integration rather than inventing a balance.</p>
    <h2>Reconcile records by owner and channel</h2>
    <p>Inventory held exports, invoices, notices and destination records. For each field name the source of truth: Shopify customer identity, retained loyalty balance, review status or destination delivery status. Match customer IDs as well as email and phone; preserve changed addresses and unresolved duplicates. Record who can correct a disputed value.</p><p>Separate email and SMS subscription states and retain source, timestamp, disclosure evidence and exclusions where available. Import withdrawals before building sending audiences. Counts are a reconciliation aid, not proof of eligibility. If old access is unavailable, list missing evidence and ask the responsible provider what recovery is possible; do not promise an export or reconstruct permission from purchase history. See <a href="/guides/consent">permission evidence</a>.</p>
    <h2>Repair capture and the customer contact endpoint</h2>
    <p>Trace old popups, checkout fields, packaging QR codes, keywords and signup links to a supported receiving service. Submit controlled email-only, text-only and withdrawn profiles. Inspect the destination record, incentive and source evidence. Remove or replace instructions that still point to an inactive endpoint.</p><p>Obtain provider confirmation of number ownership, transfer outcome, registration and active reply routing. A number stored in an export is not a completed port. Exercise STOP, HELP and an ordinary question on the active supported path and verify the responsible staff inbox. Preserve unresolved service conversations and an alternative contact route when history cannot be recovered. Keep required order updates with their actual service owner rather than turning a promotional offer into a supposed service message.</p>
    <h2>Demonstrate continuity with controlled events</h2>
    <p>Ask <a href="/apps/attentive">Attentive</a> and <a href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend</a> to demonstrate the retained integration relevant to your account; compare <a href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a> or <a href="/apps/postscript">Postscript</a> against the same job where appropriate. A <a href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy evaluation</a> must prove its own delivery and data path. No candidate inherits automatic compatibility from its name.</p><p>Use a fresh controlled order, duplicate event, delayed purchase, cancellation and withdrawal during a wait. Check customer matching, review-request deduplication, reward-link validity and purchase exits. Classify historical queues as already completed, cancelled, recreated once or unavailable. Historical imports must not start fresh welcome sequences. If acceptance fails, pause that path and return to a known supported configuration; retired messaging is not a rollback destination.</p><p>Preserve campaign exercises as proposals: a 4,200-person waitlist for 80 units, VIP access without codes, variant-aware sold-out cancellation and city-specific local timing. Separate gift and self-purchase needs, exclude active subscribers from unrelated flash offers and retain style/value preferences. Keep the next quarter’s launch, replenishment and shipping calendar with one sender per job. These fixtures establish questions to test, not claimed results.</p>
    <h2>Price retained products and replacement delivery separately</h2>
    <p>Compare current quotes for supported delivery, retained Reviews/Loyalty, integration maintenance, staff support and recovery work. Include quiet and peak volume, contact growth, message encoding and segments, destination rates, carrier fees, registration and overlap. Track old billing disputes and closure independently. Neither deprecation nor a new contract proves every old invoice is settled.</p><p>For illustration, 100 gross less a 10 incentive and 45 variable costs leaves 45 before messaging and support. Net sales of 90 less 45 gives the same result; do not subtract the discount twice. Compare contribution with a suitable holdout and consistent refund windows. Archive old attribution definitions rather than presenting a reporting reset as growth. Use <a href="/guides/pricing">cost modeling</a> and <a href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline</a>.</p>
    <h2>Accept the supported operation and its remaining exceptions</h2>
    <p>Keep a handover register for retained product settings, current forms, customer identity, channel permissions, active sender, replies and every event queue. Give unresolved records a named owner and next action. Preserve required service work while holding campaigns whose eligibility or destination is uncertain.</p><p>Before release check stock, offer expiry, recipient-time scheduling, combined frequency and current exclusions. Set audience-specific stop rules using <a href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a>, <a href="/guides/quiet-hours">timing</a> and <a href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">coordination</a>. Accept a replacement when observed destination evidence meets the written brief; do not infer readiness from equal imported totals or an arbitrary calendar deadline.</p>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
